<h1 class="text-heading font-semibold mb-4">Configuration</h1>
<p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
  Instance settings (<code>server_config</code>). Edit OIDC claim and role mapping via
  their dedicated pages. To offer the OAuth 2.0 API, see
  <a href="#oauth-switch" class="link link-primary">OAuth 2.0 authorization server</a> below.
</p>

<p :if={Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :info)} class="alert alert-success mb-4" role="status">
  {Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :info)}
</p>
<p :if={Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :error)} class="alert alert-error mb-4" role="alert">
  {Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :error)}
</p>

<%!-- OIDC scopes: POST form (story configurable-oidc-scopes, AC7/AC8).
      Operators change scope strings at runtime — no redeploy needed.
      openid is always included by scope_list/0 and admin_oidc_scope/0. --%>
<form id="oidc-scopes-form" method="post" action="/admin/config/scopes" class="mb-6">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="hidden" name="_click_proof" value="" data-click-proof />
  <h2 class="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">OIDC scopes</h2>

  <label class="form-control mt-2">
    <span class="label-text">Matrix client scopes</span>
    <input
      type="text"
      name="matrix_oidc_extra_scopes"
      aria-label="Matrix client scopes"
      value={scope_value(@config, "matrix_oidc_extra_scopes")}
      placeholder="profile email"
      class="input input-bordered"
    />
    <span class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
      Space-separated scope names. <code>openid</code> is always included.
    </span>
  </label>

  <label class="form-control mt-2">
    <span class="label-text">Admin client scopes</span>
    <input
      type="text"
      name="admin_oidc_extra_scopes"
      aria-label="Admin client scopes"
      value={scope_value(@config, "admin_oidc_extra_scopes")}
      placeholder="profile email groups"
      class="input input-bordered"
    />
    <span class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
      Space-separated scope names. <code>openid</code> is always included.
    </span>
  </label>

  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-3">Save scopes</button>
</form>

<%!-- SSO redirect schemes: POST form (story fix-and-configure-sso-redirect-schemes,
      AC8/AC9). Additional client deep-link schemes allowed as redirectUrl on
      GET /_matrix/client/v3/login/sso/redirect, beyond the hardcoded defaults
      (element, schildichat, im.fluffychat.auth). No redeploy needed. --%>
<form id="sso-schemes-form" method="post" action="/admin/config/sso-schemes" class="mb-6">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="hidden" name="_click_proof" value="" data-click-proof />
  <h2 class="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">SSO redirect schemes</h2>

  <label class="form-control mt-2">
    <span class="label-text">Additional SSO redirect schemes</span>
    <input
      type="text"
      name="sso_extra_redirect_schemes"
      aria-label="Additional SSO redirect schemes"
      value={sso_schemes_value(@config, "sso_extra_redirect_schemes")}
      placeholder="myorg-matrix, custom-app"
      class="input input-bordered"
    />
    <span class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
      Comma-separated scheme names (case-insensitive, alphanumeric + dash/dot/plus only).
      Examples: element, schildichat, im.fluffychat.auth, myorg-matrix. Hardcoded denylist
      (javascript, data, file, vbscript, blob) cannot be overridden.
    </span>
  </label>

  <p id="sso-schemes-reauth-hint" class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/70">
    Saving this setting needs a fresh sign-in. If you are asked to sign in again, you return to this page and must enter your change again.
  </p>
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-3" aria-describedby="sso-schemes-reauth-hint">Save SSO schemes</button>
</form>

<%!-- SSO redirect origins: POST form (story legacy-sso-redirect-confirmation, G3-3, D14). The https origins whose
      legacy SSO logins skip the confirmation page. Validated by Nebu.Matrix.normalize_sso_redirect_origins/1. --%>
<form id="sso-origins-form" method="post" action="/admin/config/sso-origins" class="mb-6">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="hidden" name="_click_proof" value="" data-click-proof />
  <h2 class="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">SSO redirect origins</h2>

  <div class="form-control mt-2">
    <label for="sso-origins-input" class="label-text">Allowed SSO redirect origins</label>
    <input
      type="text"
      id="sso-origins-input"
      name="sso_redirect_allowed_origins"
      value={sso_origins_input_value(assigns, @config)}
      placeholder="https://element.example.com, https://app.element.io"
      aria-describedby={sso_origins_describedby(assigns)}
      aria-invalid={if assigns[:sso_origins_error], do: "true"}
      class="input input-bordered"
    />
    <p :if={assigns[:sso_origins_error]} id="sso-origins-error" role="alert" class="mt-1 text-error">
      {assigns[:sso_origins_error]}
    </p>
    <div id="sso-origins-help" class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
      <p>Comma-separated https origins (scheme, host and optional port; no path or wildcard).</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Only list origins you control.</strong>
        Listed origins skip the confirmation page and receive a sign-in token with full access to the account.
      </p>
      <p>Always allowed without listing:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          the server origin <code>{sso_server_origin()}</code>. It must be an origin you control, which matters when
          the server name is delegated via .well-known to another host;
        </li>
        <li>the OAuth issuer origin, when configured;</li>
        <li>
          the registered redirect URIs of approved OAuth clients, and every path below them (not the rest of their
          origin). Their legacy logins get a full, unscoped session.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Other https origins see a confirmation page on every login. App schemes such as element:// are
        configured in the SSO redirect schemes form above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p id="sso-origins-reauth-hint" class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/70">
    Saving this setting needs a fresh sign-in. If you are asked to sign in again, you return to this page and must enter your change again.
  </p>
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-3" aria-describedby="sso-origins-reauth-hint">Save SSO origins</button>
</form>

<%!-- OIDC refresh mode: POST form. Two native <select>s (Matrix + admin),
      mirroring the bootstrap wizard contract (story oidc-refresh-mode-config,
      AC5/AC6). Operators change either client's mode at runtime — no redeploy. --%>
<form id="oidc-refresh-mode-form" method="post" action="/admin/config/refresh-mode" class="mb-6">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="hidden" name="_click_proof" value="" data-click-proof />
  <h2 class="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">OIDC refresh mode</h2>

  <label class="form-control mt-2">
    <span class="label-text">Matrix client refresh mode</span>
    <select name="matrix_oidc_refresh_mode" aria-label="Matrix refresh mode" class="select select-bordered">
      <option value="offline" selected={refresh_mode(@config, "matrix_oidc_refresh_mode") == "offline"}>
        offline (offline_access)
      </option>
      <option value="online" selected={refresh_mode(@config, "matrix_oidc_refresh_mode") == "online"}>
        online
      </option>
    </select>
  </label>

  <label class="form-control mt-2">
    <span class="label-text">Admin client refresh mode</span>
    <select name="admin_oidc_refresh_mode" aria-label="Admin refresh mode" class="select select-bordered">
      <option value="offline" selected={refresh_mode(@config, "admin_oidc_refresh_mode") == "offline"}>
        offline (offline_access)
      </option>
      <option value="online" selected={refresh_mode(@config, "admin_oidc_refresh_mode") == "online"}>
        online
      </option>
    </select>
  </label>

  <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-2">
    <strong>offline</strong>: long-lived offline refresh token (survives IdP logout).
    <strong>online</strong>: session-bound refresh token (dies on IdP SSO logout).
    <strong>Dex issues a refresh token only when <code>offline_access</code> is requested</strong>
    — so in online mode refresh is disabled on Dex (use offline for Dex).
  </p>

  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-3">Save refresh mode</button>
</form>

<%!-- OAuth 2.0 authorization server: the Admin UI writer of `oauth_enabled` / `oauth_issuer_url` (story admin-oauth-switch,
      AS1-AS12). The same protection as the SSO trust forms (strict fetch metadata + the Safari click proof, a fresh admin
      sign-in, no framing); switching on needs the acknowledgement; one audit row per change. The status list is derived by the
      server (Nebu.Admin.OAuthSwitch.status/2): every item starts with a word, never colour only. --%>
<section id="oauth-switch" aria-labelledby="oauth-switch-heading" class="mb-6">
  <h2 id="oauth-switch-heading" class="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">OAuth 2.0 authorization server</h2>
  <p class="text-text-secondary mb-2">
    Nebu can act as an OAuth 2.0 authorization server in front of your identity provider (Matrix 1.15 clients such as
    current Element Web and Element X sign in through it). It is off by default; the stored setting is shown under Status. Read the
    activation checklist first: <code>docs/architecture/07-deployment.md</code>, section "Activating OAuth".
  </p>

  <h3 id="oauth-status-heading" class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-1">Status</h3>
  <ul id="oauth-status" aria-labelledby="oauth-status-heading" class="list-disc pl-5 mb-2">
    <li :for={item <- @oauth_status} data-status-id={item.id} data-level={item.level} class="break-words">
      <strong>{status_word(item.level)}:</strong> {item.text}
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p id="oauth-not-checked" class="mb-3 text-sm text-base-content/70">
    The server cannot see or check everything: it cannot see your load balancer, whether the client IP addresses it forwards
    are the real ones (the positive client-IP test), what your identity provider puts into <code>auth_time</code>, or how the
    clients behave. Those, and the manual verification groups A to F of the checklist, stay your job; this list never says that
    OAuth is ready to be switched on.
  </p>

  <form id="oauth-switch-form" method="post" action="/admin/config/oauth-switch">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
    <input type="hidden" name="_click_proof" value="" data-click-proof />
    <input type="hidden" name="oauth_enabled" value="false" />

    <div class="form-control mt-2">
      <label for="oauth-enabled-input" class="label cursor-pointer justify-start gap-2 w-fit max-w-full">
        <input
          type="checkbox"
          id="oauth-enabled-input"
          name="oauth_enabled"
          value="true"
          checked={@oauth_form.enabled}
          aria-describedby={oauth_describedby("oauth-enabled-help", "oauth-enabled-error", @oauth_errors, :enabled)}
          aria-invalid={if Map.has_key?(@oauth_errors, :enabled), do: "true"}
          class="checkbox"
        />
        <span class="label-text">Offer the OAuth 2.0 API</span>
      </label>
      <p :if={@oauth_errors[:enabled]} id="oauth-enabled-error" role="alert" class="mt-1 text-error">
        {@oauth_errors[:enabled]}
      </p>
      <p id="oauth-enabled-help" class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
        Checked = on. Unchecked = off, the kill switch.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-base-content/70">
        To roll back, uncheck it and save: all nodes follow {oauth_propagation_text(@oauth_cache_ms)} (<code>NEBU_OAUTH_CONFIG_CACHE_MS</code>).
        Running OAuth sessions stay valid after you switch OAuth off until their access token expires (at most one hour); to end them
        at once run <code>revoke_all_oauth_sessions</code> as described in the checklist.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-control mt-2">
      <label for="oauth-issuer-input" class="label-text">Issuer URL</label>
      <input
        type="text"
        id="oauth-issuer-input"
        name="oauth_issuer_url"
        value={@oauth_form.issuer}
        placeholder="https://chat.example.com"
        autocomplete="off"
        spellcheck="false"
        inputmode="url"
        aria-describedby={oauth_describedby("oauth-issuer-help", "oauth-issuer-error", @oauth_errors, :issuer)}
        aria-invalid={if Map.has_key?(@oauth_errors, :issuer), do: "true"}
        class="input input-bordered w-full max-w-xl"
      />
      <p :if={@oauth_errors[:issuer]} id="oauth-issuer-error" role="alert" class="mt-1 text-error">
        {@oauth_errors[:issuer]}
      </p>
      <div id="oauth-issuer-help" class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
        <p>
          The public https address of this server as your users reach it: no path, query, fragment or user name. Without a
          valid issuer OAuth stays off, whatever the checkbox says.
        </p>
        <p>
          The origin of the issuer is also trusted by the legacy SSO login (<code>m.login.sso</code>) without a confirmation page, even while OAuth is off:
          only enter an origin you control.
        </p>
        <p :if={@oauth_form.suggested?}>
          The value is suggested, not saved yet: it is derived from <code>NEBU_SERVER_NAME</code>. Check it before you save.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-control mt-2">
      <label for="oauth-ack-input" class="label cursor-pointer justify-start gap-2 w-fit max-w-full">
        <input
          type="checkbox"
          id="oauth-ack-input"
          name="oauth_activation_ack"
          value="true"
          checked={@oauth_form.ack}
          aria-describedby={oauth_describedby("oauth-ack-help", "oauth-ack-error", @oauth_errors, :ack)}
          aria-invalid={if Map.has_key?(@oauth_errors, :ack), do: "true"}
          class="checkbox"
        />
        <span class="label-text">I have read the activation checklist and know that unchecking the switch turns OAuth off, while the issuer origin stays trusted by the legacy SSO login until I clear the issuer</span>
      </label>
      <p :if={@oauth_errors[:ack]} id="oauth-ack-error" role="alert" class="mt-1 text-error">
        {@oauth_errors[:ack]}
      </p>
      <p id="oauth-ack-help" class="label-text-alt mt-1 text-base-content/70">
        Required when you switch OAuth on, or set or change the issuer (also while OAuth is off).
      </p>
    </div>

    <p id="oauth-switch-reauth-hint" class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/70">
      Saving this setting needs a fresh sign-in. If you are asked to sign in again, you return to this page and must enter your change again.
    </p>
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-3" aria-describedby="oauth-switch-reauth-hint">Save OAuth settings</button>
  </form>
</section>

<div class="overflow-x-auto">
  <table class="table table-zebra">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr :for={{k, v} <- @config}>
        <td class="font-mono text-mono">{k}</td>
        <td class="font-mono text-mono break-all">{v}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
